      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Considering snow load, it's generally recommended to increase the beam size haunch (where it flares outward at the post) by at least 25% to account for the increased load. This extra capacity is known as the \"hunch\" or \"ripening factor\" and helps prevent beam sagging or failure under the added weight. Typical hunch values range from 25% to 50% for snow-loaded decks, depending on the local building code and extreme snow load conditions.",
